{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Record the architectural decision behind three changes to a committed, shared store format plus a\nfield deletion, so the mixed-version protocol and each rollback boundary are discoverable. session_log **1cb6-d553-6565-49b4** (measured facts; do not re-derive).\n\n## Content required\n- The three committed-format changes — **A2** (`last_get_pass` relocation), **A3** (baseline\n  normalization), **A4-2** (prev key-set) — plus the `baseline_advanced_at` deletion (A1).\n- Why the cache stays committed on-branch at all (ephemeral GHA runners; epic 6c9c dropped WS-1).\n- The mixed-version protocol: write-new / read-`max()` / delete-later, and why `max()` rather than\n  first-wins.\n- **A2-2's gate** (A2-1 on main; a successful `reconcile-bridge.yml` run on a descendant SHA; an explicitly refreshed host probe with no older process; and the old/new-writer self-healing oracle) and why a\n  pass-record version stamp could not be used.\n- Each rollback boundary: A2-1 reversible, A3 reversible via idempotent read-path canonicalization,\n  A2-2 and A4-2 irreversible with their stated preconditions.\n- Why assignee is excluded from normalization (data loss via `_assignee_candidates`).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] An ADR file exists under `adr/` with the next sequential number, enumerating all three\n      committed-format changes, the deletion, the mixed-version protocol, the A2-2 gate, and each\n      rollback boundary. Tier: **doc-existence + content check** (grep for each required element).\n- [ ] It cites the measured numbers (12.79 -> 1.74 KB marginal; 218/399 identical prev key sets) and\n      links session_log **1cb6-d553-6565-49b4** (measured facts; do not re-derive).\n- [ ] `docs/` index and any ADR list are updated so it is reachable. Verify: link check.\n\n## Files\n`adr/00XX-bridge-state-format-changes.md`, `adr/README.md` or index\n\nScope: S. Depends on A3 and A4-2 (so it documents the final shapes)."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785785409342096001,"uuid":"9ed725f9-1e25-444f-afbd-64d7e12f95a0"}